//--- Yaw:

Yaw is a side-to-side movement of an airplane's nose, caused by the deflection of the rudder.

Yaw is one of three dimensions of motion for an airplane, along with pitch and roll.

The other two dimensions are: 
Pitch: An up or down movement of the nose
Roll: An up and down movement of the wing tips

The yaw axis is the line perpendicular to the plane of the wings, and the airplane rotates around this axis to turn. To visualize yaw, you can imagine standing on the balls of your feet and twisting your weight from side to side.

Yaw can be difficult to visualize because it involves movement along the z-axis.
